# "The serial mirror" — POKE 774,2 on a video console sends what the screen
# prints down the serial line too.
#
# The expect and absent lines read the serial line, not the screen: a video
# case that names a `wait` waits for it there. The table and the OK after it
# arrive; the RUN typed before line 20 does not, because every boot leaves the
# mirror off. The screen shows the same table, which CLS cleared the way for
# without sending anything down the line.
console video
wait OK
expect ^SEVEN TIMES TABLE$
expect ^ 1 X 7 = 7\s*$
expect ^ 5 X 7 = 35\s*$
absent ^RUN
screen ^SEVEN TIMES TABLE\s*$
screen ^ 5 X 7 = 35\s*$
